1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,069
Chai Corner now has five
outlets and a small head office.

2
00:00:04,369 --> 00:00:07,099
But every small decision
still waits for Ravi.

3
00:00:07,649 --> 00:00:10,698
At the bus stand, a
customer wants a refund.

4
00:00:10,698 --> 00:00:11,961
Meena calls Ravi.

5
00:00:12,261 --> 00:00:13,731
The milk runs low.

6
00:00:13,731 --> 00:00:15,465
Meena calls Ravi again.

7
00:00:15,765 --> 00:00:18,838
Ravi gets forty calls a
day, and customers wait.

8
00:00:19,488 --> 00:00:21,834
So Ravi visits the bus stand outlet.

9
00:00:22,184 --> 00:00:25,620
He hands Meena a clipboard,
and a key to the cash drawer.

10
00:00:25,970 --> 00:00:27,700
The clipboard is the job.

11
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,670
Keep this outlet running well.

12
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:32,159
The key is the power to decide.

13
00:00:32,159 --> 00:00:35,415
From today, you approve
refunds and order supplies.

14
00:00:36,065 --> 00:00:38,385
This is delegation of authority.

15
00:00:38,685 --> 00:00:43,285
Delegation means a manager gives a
team member the authority to do a task,

16
00:00:43,285 --> 00:00:44,953
and to decide about it.

17
00:00:45,553 --> 00:00:47,241
The manager shares the work.

18
00:00:47,241 --> 00:00:49,120
He does not walk away from it.

19
00:00:49,770 --> 00:00:52,323
Watch one refund, before delegation.

20
00:00:52,672 --> 00:00:54,047
The customer asks.

21
00:00:54,047 --> 00:00:57,755
Meena phones head office,
and waits behind four calls.

22
00:00:58,105 --> 00:01:00,765
Ravi says yes, and the refund is given.

23
00:01:00,765 --> 00:01:01,837
Twenty minutes.

24
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:04,568
Now the same refund, after delegation.

25
00:01:04,568 --> 00:01:07,423
The customer asks, and
Meena checks her limit.

26
00:01:07,773 --> 00:01:09,614
Refund given in one minute.

27
00:01:09,614 --> 00:01:11,504
No phone call, no waiting.

28
00:01:12,154 --> 00:01:14,482
Delegation has three linked parts.

29
00:01:14,832 --> 00:01:15,732
One.

30
00:01:15,338 --> 00:01:17,777
Responsibility, the job to be done.

31
00:01:17,777 --> 00:01:20,424
Meena must keep the outlet running well.

32
00:01:20,774 --> 00:01:21,674
Two.

33
00:01:21,305 --> 00:01:23,595
Authority, the power to decide.

34
00:01:23,595 --> 00:01:26,051
Meena can approve a refund herself.

35
00:01:26,401 --> 00:01:27,301
Three.

36
00:01:27,025 --> 00:01:29,570
Accountability, answering for results.

37
00:01:29,570 --> 00:01:32,137
Every Friday, Meena reports to Ravi.

38
00:01:32,787 --> 00:01:33,998
Now the key rule.

39
00:01:33,998 --> 00:01:36,086
What moves down, and what stays?

40
00:01:36,436 --> 00:01:38,014
Authority moves down.

41
00:01:38,014 --> 00:01:39,881
Ravi passes it to Meena.

42
00:01:40,231 --> 00:01:43,311
Responsibility is assigned,
and Meena accepts it.

43
00:01:43,661 --> 00:01:46,057
But accountability cannot be passed on.

44
00:01:46,407 --> 00:01:50,107
If the bus stand has a bad
month, Meena answers to Ravi.

45
00:01:50,107 --> 00:01:52,813
Ravi still answers for all of Chai Corner.

46
00:01:53,463 --> 00:01:55,395
You can hand over authority.

47
00:01:55,395 --> 00:01:57,061
But never accountability.

48
00:01:57,761 --> 00:01:58,960
One more rule.

49
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:00,754
The principle of parity.

50
00:02:00,754 --> 00:02:03,184
Authority must match responsibility.

51
00:02:03,534 --> 00:02:07,688
If Meena must stock the milk but
cannot spend a rupee, she will fail.

52
00:02:08,038 --> 00:02:10,686
If she can spend any
amount, money gets wasted.

53
00:02:11,036 --> 00:02:14,451
So Ravi sets a limit of
five thousand rupees a day.

54
00:02:14,451 --> 00:02:16,376
Enough power, and no more.

55
00:02:17,026 --> 00:02:19,006
Where do you see this at work today?

56
00:02:19,356 --> 00:02:20,515
Responsibility.

57
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:23,947
A shift supervisor must
open the store on time.

58
00:02:24,297 --> 00:02:25,197
Authority.

59
00:02:25,159 --> 00:02:28,713
A hotel receptionist can
waive a late checkout fee.

60
00:02:29,063 --> 00:02:30,149
Accountability.

61
00:02:30,149 --> 00:02:33,995
A project lead presents the
results at the monthly review.

62
00:02:34,345 --> 00:02:35,245
Parity.

63
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:38,396
A buyer gets a spending limit
that matches the orders.

64
00:02:39,046 --> 00:02:41,652
So why do some managers not delegate?

65
00:02:41,652 --> 00:02:42,758
Often, fear.

66
00:02:43,108 --> 00:02:44,181
The good side.

67
00:02:44,181 --> 00:02:48,176
It frees the manager, grows the
team, and speeds up decisions.

68
00:02:48,526 --> 00:02:54,769
In a 2015 Gallup study of 143 chief
executives, strong delegators grew

69
00:02:54,769 --> 00:02:56,155
much faster.

70
00:02:56,505 --> 00:02:57,574
The hard side.

71
00:02:57,574 --> 00:03:01,654
Letting go feels risky, and people
make mistakes while they learn.

72
00:03:02,004 --> 00:03:04,198
Work can also creep back up.

73
00:03:04,198 --> 00:03:09,309
In 1974, the Harvard Business Review
called it the monkey on your back.

74
00:03:09,659 --> 00:03:11,678
Meena says, we have a problem.

75
00:03:11,678 --> 00:03:13,889
Ravi says, let me think about it.

76
00:03:13,889 --> 00:03:15,670
Now Ravi carries the monkey.

77
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:19,698
The lesson: let go of the task,
but keep an eye on the result.

78
00:03:20,348 --> 00:03:21,320
Quick check.

79
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:23,373
Meena approves a wrong refund.

80
00:03:23,373 --> 00:03:25,365
Who is ultimately accountable?

81
00:03:27,265 --> 00:03:28,165
Ravi!

82
00:03:27,921 --> 00:03:30,541
Accountability cannot be delegated.

83
00:03:31,141 --> 00:03:32,150
So, remember.

84
00:03:32,450 --> 00:03:37,145
Delegation gives a team member the
authority to do a task, and to decide.

85
00:03:37,495 --> 00:03:42,271
It links responsibility, authority and
accountability, with authority matching

86
00:03:42,271 --> 00:03:43,350
responsibility.

87
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:45,230
Authority moves down.

88
00:03:45,230 --> 00:03:47,764
Accountability stays with the manager.

89
00:03:48,364 --> 00:03:51,975
Next time, how much power
should stay at head office?

90
00:03:51,975 --> 00:03:54,211
Centralization and decentralization.
